      "kind": "culture",
      "title": "du to everyone",
      "text": "Marta is a shopkeeper and Sam a customer, but they still say \"du\" (\"you\") to each other. Norwegian has an old polite word, \"De\", but almost nobody uses it today: \"du\" is for everyone, even a teacher or a shop assistant. \"Vær så god\" is what you say when you hand something over; it means \"here you are\" or \"please, go ahead\".",
